# Model config: Qwen3.8-27B with static YaRN for ~1M context -- model-intrinsic.
#
# Same BF16 weights as models/qwen3.8-27b.env, plus rope scaling. Native context
# is 262,144 (GGUF qwen35.context_length); YaRN x4 extends it to ~1,048,576.
#
# Upstream publishes the extension as a rope_parameters override on
# text_config:
#     rope_type: "yarn", factor: 4.0, original_max_position_embeddings: 262144,
#     rope_theta: 10000000, partial_rotary_factor: 0.25,
#     mrope_interleaved: true, mrope_section: [11, 11, 10]
# Only the first three map to llama.cpp CLI flags (--rope-scaling / --rope-scale
# / --yarn-orig-ctx). The rest are ALREADY BAKED INTO THE GGUF and must not be
# re-specified: rope_theta      == qwen35.rope.freq_base       = 1e7
#              mrope_section    == qwen35.rope.dimension_sections = [11,11,10,0]
#              partial_rotary   == rope.dimension_count 64 / head_dim 256 = 0.25
# Verified against the GGUF metadata on 2026-08-14.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE CONFIG: static YaRN applies to EVERY request and upstream warns
# it degrades short-context quality. Keep the unscaled qwen3.8-27b config for
# day-to-day work and launch this one only when you actually need >262K.
# For a ~524,288 target use --rope-scale 2 instead of 4 (upstream calls this out
# explicitly) -- less short-context damage for the context you actually need.
#
# Sampling / vision / thinking-control: see models/qwen3.8-27b.env.

: "${MODEL:=Qwen3.8-27B/BF16/Qwen3.8-27B-BF16-00001-of-00002.gguf}"

LLAMA_ARGS+=(--temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0 --presence-penalty 0.0 --repeat-penalty 1.0)
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--rope-scaling yarn --rope-scale 4 --yarn-orig-ctx 262144)
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--mmproj "/models/Qwen3.8-27B/mmproj-BF16.gguf")
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--alias qwen3.8-27b-1m)
